					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anqxyr" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(966960); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=966960&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608196097" alt="anqxyr" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=966960)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anqxyr" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(966960); return false;" >anqxyr</a></span> <span class="odate time_1385670070 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">28 Nov 2013 20:21</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1903951">
									

<p>The people that approached Arkady, are they supposed to be CI? It's not very clear, they come across as generic villains. The bit about efficiency is what made me think of Insurgency.</p>
<p>&quot;caressed his cheek with a single slender digit&quot;. That broke my disbelief. I just can't imagine a person acting like that, given a situation.</p>
<p>So, Arkady &quot;spent years in service of the Division&quot;, yet he doesn't know about the existence of anomalous stuff. I don't really follow the portrayal of GRU-P; is this supposed to be normal for them?</p>
<p>The &quot;I will count to ten, out loud, for no discernible reason&quot; portion felt contrived to me.</p>
<p>Ultimately, I just don't care about this. No vote.</p>

