					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/crayne" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1346995); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1346995&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608196097" alt="Crayne" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1346995)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/crayne" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1346995); return false;" >Crayne</a></span> <span class="odate time_1385712636 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">29 Nov 2013 08:10</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1904223">
									

<blockquote>
<p>The people that approached Arkady, are they supposed to be CI? It's not very clear, they come across as generic villains.<br />
The bit about efficiency is what made me think of Insurgency.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not sure where you're getting that. The first part, above the line, is Arkady in 2013, running from the Foundation because he's not convinced they won't treat him badly. The second part is a flashback to 1981, when he was first recruited by GRU. The last part returns to 2013.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;caressed his cheek with a single slender digit&quot;. That broke my disbelief. I just can't imagine a person acting like that, given a situation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Well, I guess I got carried away there. You're right, will edit for a bit less purple prose.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>So, Arkady &quot;spent years in service of the Division&quot;, yet he doesn't know about the existence of anomalous stuff. I don't really follow the portrayal of GRU-P; is this supposed to be normal for them?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Arkady spent years in the service of the Division and got intimately acquainted with anomalies. But if you didn't pick up on the flashback thing and the fact that it was his recruitment by the Division, I can understand how this would make no sense whatsoever.</p>
<p>With my explanation of the different parts of the story, does it make more sense?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The &quot;I will count to ten, out loud, for no discernible reason&quot; portion felt contrived to me.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You have a point and all I have to say in defense is that it works for me as a dramatic device. Anyway, thanks for your feedback, I appreciate it. :)</p>

							</div>

								
					
